  "description": "A clever drivetrain and versatile geometry make this bike a great way to get from A-to-B. Costing less than a yearly bus pass, our Skyway 2 will make your commute a lot more fun. We have broken our entry-level urban bike out into a couple tiers, making a quality ride even more accessible. This level 2 Skyway uses Shimano’s Cues drivetrain, offering proven performance and easy maintenance. Powerful hydraulic disc brakes put a ton of stopping power right at your fingertips and are a real step up from rim brakes – especially on rainy days. Built on a light and strong aluminum frame, the Skyway series has a comfortable upright riding position that’s great for urban environments. Rack and fender mounts let you customize your ride and make it more useful. And the large-diameter wheels carry more momentum than standard 26in. mountain bike wheels, so you cruise right over bumps, rough pavement and unpaved side streets.\n\nFrame uses 6000 series butted aluminum tubing, giving it an excellent strength to weight ratio\n\n700 x 40mm high-volume tires help smooth out rough surfaces and can handle dirt roads, paths and light trail use\n\nShimano MT201 hydraulic disc brakes provide outstanding stopping power in all weather conditions\n\n2 x 10-speed Shimano Cues drivetrain provides smooth, reliable shifting, giving a great range for trails or hills\n\nThe Cues line provides reliable performance, durability, and easy maintenance – with cross compatibility across the line\n\nUpright seated position and 25mm riser bars give you good visibility in traffic\n\nComposite flat pedals are easy to use in a wide rang of footwear, from business casual to flip-flops\n\nBikes are covered by MEC's Rocksolid Guarantee and Bike Service Agreement. You can bring your bike to any MEC bike shop for free adjustments and minor maintenance for a year after purchase\n\nMEC bikes are designed in Canada. Everything from the frames to the graphics were developed at the MEC Head Office in Vancouver, BC\n\nDue to challenges with supply chain, components may be substituted for comparable parts at any time. The listed build is how MEC intended your bike to arrive, though the manufacturer may need to make a tweak or two to get you riding sooner",
